## 2026-09-22 — PvP damage never worked: the friendly-fire check; props gate

- **PvP gun damage was IMPOSSIBLE by construction**: `GunCombat.TallyHit`'s
  same-team guard (`theirs.CombatTeam == CombatTeam`) ate every shot — both
  players' guns default to team 0 and nothing online ever set the puppet's
  team. Training bots only worked because EnemyController sets team 1. Found
  via game logs (a whole 157 s match with ZERO `[Gun] HIT` lines) + a headless
  repro (`test/TestTask.cs`): raw ray hit the puppet, combat path dropped it.
  Fix: arena sets `_puppet.Gun.CombatTeam = 1` at spawn. Repro now prints HIT.
- **Arena props ("middle area still old")**: `PropLibrary.PropsAvailable`
  probed `System.IO.Directory.Exists(GlobalizePath("res://assets/glb/props"))`
  — permanently false inside an export, so props were disabled in every
  exported build ("[PropLibrary] assets/glb/props absent" in the logs).
  ResourceLoader probe first now; raw-dir probe kept for un-imported dev drops.
- **props_hires red herring**: the game reads `assets/glb/props` (8.5 MB,
  imported, packed all along) — NOT `props_hires` (661 MB raw AI meshes,
  ~41 MB per prop, uniformly undecimated). Re-added the props_hires
  `.gdignore`; exe back to 756 MB from 2.34 GB. If hires ever ships, it needs
  a decimation pass first (goblet at 42.9 MB says everything).
- The `.png.jpg` / `.jpg.jpg` mats ERROR stacks in exported logs are NOISE:
  the double extensions are the real on-disk filenames (bulk png→jpg convert
  kept old names), the files are imported/packed, and the failed line is just
  the source-file attempt before the resource-loader fallback succeeds.

