## 2026-09-22 — Render playtest round 3: the real asset/body root causes

- **"Floating hands" opponent (THE fix)**: every player body is put on visual
  layer 2 so its own FP camera can cull it (`CullMask ~2u`) — but nothing ever
  re-layered a PUPPET, so the opponent's body was invisible to your FP camera
  BY CONSTRUCTION; only their weapon rig (other layer) rendered. The
  `IsRemotePuppet` setter now flips `_playerBody` to world layer 1. Test
  harnesses never caught it because their own cameras see all layers.
- **"Old textures / missing design" (exports only)**: a bug CLASS — code that
  loads assets by reading SOURCE files (`Image.Load` on globalized paths,
  `GltfDocument.AppendFromFile`) works in editor runs but fails silently in
  exports, which pack only the IMPORTED artifacts. Added ResourceLoader
  fallbacks (`GD.Load<Texture2D>().GetImage()` + `Decompress()`) in
  DungeonBuilder (wall/floor mats), ArenaBuilder (night sky, grass, wood),
  ManorFurniture (paintings), PieceVariants (carpets). PropLibrary and
  HallwayDemo already did resource-first — the correct pattern to copy.
  Verified the pck actually CONTAINS the assets (byte-scanned the exe), so
  packing was never the issue — loading was.
- **Loadout race**: client's `{"t":"loadout"}` can arrive before its arena
  builds; the roll is now buffered (`_rolledStarterIdx/_rolledArenaIdx`) and
  re-applied after spawn — both players always get identical guns.
- **Puppet's duplicate HUD**: PlayerHUD hides itself when its parent is a
  remote puppet (was drawing a second, frozen ammo counter over the real one).
- **Title-screen population counter died after one match**: TitleScreen
  subscribed `NetworkManager.StatsUpdated` (autoload) and never unsubscribed —
  the disposed handler broke the emission for the NEXT title screen. Added
  `_ExitTree` unsubscribe (PlayGameScreen already did this correctly).
- **Side-by-side testing**: `--test-windowed` flag (GameSettings applies
  Windowed 960×540 regardless of the saved fullscreen pref, without writing
