## 2026-09-22 — Render playtest round 2: latency-real fixes

- **NEVER run headless `--import`/`--export` while the editor is open.** The
  5:13 PM export shipped without the UAL character model (opponent = floating
  hands + gun) and with stale textures — two Godot instances fighting over
  `.godot/imported/` corrupts the cache. The missing model then cascaded:
  wonky gun seating, no red outline (no skinned meshes), and shots missing
  (players aim at the visuals, which had detached from the physics capsule).
  Export checklist is now: close editor → `--import` → `--export-release`.
- **Hit-validation window 300→750 ms** (`HitClaimWindowMs`, buffer 24→48
  slots): 300 ms was shorter than real one-way relay latency, so every
  moving-target hit through Render was rejected — playtested as "guns do no
  damage". The claim references the victim's own broadcast trail, so the
  1.5 m tolerance stays tight; only the window needed latency headroom.
- **Claim latch**: `WeaponPickup` no longer re-arms `_claimSent` on key
  release — one claim in flight until the verdict consumes the pickup, label
  shows "Claiming..." during the host round trip (was: E-spam, one relay
  message per press).
- **Wallhack marker survives a missing model**: the red diamond is built
  unconditionally; only the skinned outline is best-effort (warns instead of
  silently dropping the whole marked package).
- **Role banners**: small persistent top-right text for the whole hunt —
  "HUNTER — kill them before the timer ends" / "BEING HUNTED — survive till
  the end of the timer". Freed in ResolveMatch.
- **Clock-race disconnect**: both clients run their own 40 s timers and the
  first to expire disconnects the relay, so the slower client saw "Opponent
  left.". `OnPeerDisconnected` now resolves as the clock outcome when the
  local timer has ≤3 s left. "Hunt Failed" renamed "Failed to kill".

