primitives driven by tweens, everything frees itself:
- **Travelling tracer** (`TracerStreak`): a short bright core+glow streak flown
  muzzle→impact at 320 m/s. An instant line reads as a laser; a moving streak
  reads as a bullet. Damage stays instant — only the visual travels, and the
  impact visual fires when the streak ARRIVES (the slight travel beat every
  modern shooter fakes). Shotguns tracer every 3rd pellet.
- **Muzzle flash**: small emissive billboard + light + a smoke wisp, ~50 ms.
  Deliberately smaller than the old head-height light — punctuation, not the
  sentence. Scaled up for shotgun/rockets.
- **Shell casings**: tumbling brass fleck ejected from the ACTION (muzzle −0.35
  along the barrel), tween arc to the floor.
- **Backblast** for rocket tubes: smoke vented backward on launch — the
  signature of a recoilless weapon.
- **Impact**: spark + dust along the reversed shot direction.

**Rockets launch from the tube**, not the eye — flight line starts at the muzzle
and converges onto the camera ray's direction.

Note for reading captures: your OWN tracer when aiming dead-on is nearly
invisible (collinear with the eye line) — physically correct; it reads from
every other angle, verified in the TP capture (smoke, casing, streak all at the
weapon).

## Arena: wall furniture clearance contract (the real "you go into the books" fix)

Follow-up playtest: "the bookshelves are still collidable, you go into them."
The previous pass smoothed the collision ring; that was not the bug.

### Cause: props scaled uniformly into the wrong shape

`bookrow_a` is raw `1.00 long x 0.345 deep x 0.303 tall`. `AddBookshelfRing`
scaled it **uniformly** by `boardLen / longestAxis` (=5.46) to span the bay,
which also inflated depth to **1.88m** and height to 1.65m. Every "row of books"
was a 1.9m-deep slab standing out of the shelf, past the collider, into the
arena. Same class of bug on `column_a`: 0.376 wide x 1.0 tall, scaled uniformly
by 14 to reach the dome spring, ends up **5.3m wide**.

### Fix

- **Per-axis fitting.** Each axis gets its own budget (`RowDepth` 0.40,
  `RowHeight` 1.05, length → `boardLen`) instead of one uniform factor. Zero
  runtime cost: same instance count, same MultiMesh draw call. Tiling extra
  copies was rejected — bookrows are ~3000 tris and 1260 instances is already
  3.8M triangles.
- **Clearance contract** (constants + comment in ArenaBuilder): everything
  wall-mounted must sit outside `Apothem - ShelfDepth`, where the collider is.
- `TierLedge` inner radius was 28.4 — 0.9m *inside* the collider. Pulled back.
- `BalustradeR` 29.0 → 29.56.
- `ShelfOverrun` 1.7m: the collision face now continues above `topY`, covering
  the corner posts (which run to topY+0.8) and the ledge/balustrade band.
  Previously the chamfer ramped away at topY and left all of it unbacked.
- `PostClearance` 0.06m: corner posts sit at bay VERTICES, not on the chord, so
  they reach ~43mm inside the chord-derived front plane.
- `RowUnderhang` 0.6m: bookrow GLB origins are centred, so the lowest row of
  each tier hangs ~0.13m below its tier base, into the inter-tier band.
- **Doorway skip alignment (subtle).** `AddShelfCollision` evaluated
  AddBookshelfRing's `|midAngle| < openHalfAngle * 1.7` test per fine SEGMENT.
  That threshold is a per-BAY tolerance (bay mid-angles are 0.196 rad apart, so
  it skips exactly one bay); applied to 0.025-rad segments it opened 0.34 rad —
  1.7 bays — leaving the collider missing beside each doorway while shelves were
  still visible there. Now tested on the segment's owning bay (`seg / ColSubdiv`).
- Balustrades/columns now skip doorway bays too, matching the shelf ring.

### Verification — `test/TestArenaProtrusion.cs` (new)

Compares every visual vertex against the collision surface per (sector, height)
and names the offending node. This is the permanent gate for the contract; run
it after touching any prop scale or wall-decor radius.

Progression: **444 → 176 → 35 → 0** protruding cells. Worst offender went
1381mm (bookrow) → 0. The 35 remaining are all in the two open doorway bays and
are reported separately, not as failure — the ring is open there by design.

Regression: `TestShelfSlide` still PASS (2mm wobble, 0 snags);
`TestShelfCollision` still PASS — its `ShelfFrontR` expectation was updated for
`PostClearance` (it had gone `matches=False` while still reporting PASS).

### Deliberately NOT fixed

`column_a` protrudes **4453mm** — the single worst offender. Its capitals are
standable platforms (`ColumnTop*`) sized off that 5.3m width, so narrowing it
silently breaks the platforming route up the shaft. It is excluded from the gate
with a comment pointing here. Fixing it means either giving the column body
collision or re-proportioning it and `ColumnTopW` together — a call for whoever
owns that feature.

