`EquipStarterGun` already filled SECONDARY and `EquipArenaGun` PRIMARY, so the
requested rule was implemented. What was missing is that the rule was only
*implied by which method got called*: a gun added to the wrong pool would have
silently occupied the wrong hand. `GunDef.Slot` (new `GunSlot` enum) makes it
data, and TestGunSlots asserts pools and slots agree and never overlap.

